Proposed local patch to CAPD 6.1.0 (commit 03dc5628203334b214bb7d9fd63788a175521005). NOT APPLIED: applying it
modifies the shared CAPD build and needs the owner's approval. See README.md, "Known CAPD issue".

In crossSectionInOneStep, each Newton iteration sets bound = c(newReturnTime) and checks the sign of every component
of the vector field on that bound (vfOnBound), then intersects bound[j] with the hull of the curve at the endpoints
of the PREVIOUS window (oneStepReturnTime). The hull is a valid trim only on the window where monotonicity was
checked. The two windows coincide when the loop exits by convergence (the break), but not when it stops at the
10-iteration cap. The patch takes the endpoints of the current window.

--- a/capdDynSys/include/capd/poincare/PoincareMap_templateMembers.h
+++ b/capdDynSys/include/capd/poincare/PoincareMap_templateMembers.h
@@ -259,8 +259,11 @@
     bound = c(newReturnTime);
     vfOnBound = this->m_solver.getVectorField()(timeBeforeSection+oneStepReturnTime,bound);
-    VectorType L = c(oneStepReturnTime.left());
-    VectorType R = c(oneStepReturnTime.right());
+    // GENChase patch: trim with the endpoints of the SAME window on which monotonicity (vfOnBound) was checked.
+    // Upstream used the previous window (oneStepReturnTime), which is unsound if the Newton loop stops at its
+    // iteration cap without converging.
+    VectorType L = c(newReturnTime.left());
+    VectorType R = c(newReturnTime.right());
     for(size_type j=0;j<bound.dimension();++j){
       if(!(vfOnBound[j].contains(0.))){
         intersection(bound[j],intervalHull(L[j],R[j]),bound[j]);
